    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Your personal comprehensive insurance policy must be active. This covers liability and personal damages outside of the specific transit window, ensuring your bike remains legally protected for the duration of the entire relocation process.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>Logistical Paperwork and Bilty Requirements</h3>
<p>Beyond personal vehicle documents, formal logistics paperwork is required to track the shipment. The most critical component is the <strong>IBA-approved consignment bilty</strong>. This document acts as the official contract between you and the transporter.</p>
<p>It details the pickup address in Ahmedabad, the delivery location in Pune, the vehicle description, and the estimated transit time. Ensure all details on the bilty match your RC exactly to avoid discrepancies that could complicate the final delivery handover.</p>

<h3>100% Declared-Value Marine Transit Insurance</h3>
<p>While your personal insurance covers liability, it typically does not cover damage occurring specifically during the logistics transit phase. To mitigate this risk, you must opt for <strong>100% declared-value marine transit insurance</strong>. This specialized policy covers your bike against accidental damage, theft, or fire while it is in the custody of the transport provider.</p>
<p>By declaring the full market value of your vehicle, you ensure that any incident is compensated at 100% of the declared amount, without depreciation deductions. This layer of protection is essential for high-value motorcycles and provides complete peace of mind for the long-distance journey from Gujarat to Maharashtra.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


