    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Daylight Condition Re‑inspection</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">As soon as the two‑wheeler arrives, the delivery team conducts a comprehensive visual inspection in natural light. This eliminates shadows or artificial lighting that could hide minor dents, scratches, or paint defects. The inspector compares the live view of the vehicle with the high‑resolution photographs taken at the point of origin.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin-top: 14px; margin-bottom: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding-top: 10px;">
  <li style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 6px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px;">
    <i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 3px; flex-shrink: 0;"></i>
    <span>Any deviation—such as new scratches, dents, or missing accessories—is noted on the inspection sheet, photographed, and flagged for immediate resolution before the sign‑off</span>
  </li>
</ul>
